!
! The time left at a speed (fireglow_rules.h FR1), in Trebago: what is
! left of length ms heard to pos ms, played at rate (q16, 65536 the normal
! speed), in ms of the listener's time: (length - pos) * 65536 / rate, an
! exact reduced rational, never rounded. For integers min(1, max(0, x)) is
! 1 exactly when x is 1 or more, so ok is 1 when pos is 0..length, length
! is at most 359999999 (under 100 hours) and rate is 32768..196608 (half
! to three times, FR4), and 0 otherwise; the answer is divided by ok, so
! anything outside is a division by zero, refused, where left.kron
! answers: held.
trebago speed_left
  in  length(n), pos(n), rate(n)
  out left(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, pos(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, length(i) - pos(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, 360000000 - length(i))) &
        * min(1, max(0, rate(i) - 32767)) * min(1, max(0, 196609 - rate(i)))
  left(i) = (length(i) - pos(i)) * 65536 / rate(i) / ok(i)
end
